  i The name _foo starts with an underscore.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ declare const _foo: number;
      │               ^^^^
    3 │ const bar_: string = "";
    4 │ export const _baz = 1;
  
  i An underscore at the start or end of a name is often used to mark something as private, but it doesn't change how the code works, so it can mislead readers.
  
  i Remove the underscore from the name. For a class member that must stay private, start its name with # instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

